    "evaluator_feedback": "```\n=== NEXT ACTION DECISION ===\nDecision: partially revert\nRationale: The latest change introduced a regression: new assertion failures in assertRoleAssignmentClearance and assertDelegationClearance, which were not failing previously and are unrelated to the original Emergency mutex relaxation focus. Only the parts of the change that caused these regressions should be reverted, while retaining intended Emergency-specific fixes.\n\n=== VERIFICATION STATUS ===\n- Syntax: OK\n- Baseline: Satisfiable\n- Combined Model: Satisfiable\n- Assertions: Counterexamples (assertMutexAllowedDuringEmergency, assertRoleAssignmentClearance, assertDelegationClearance)\n- Instances: Meaningful (except EmergencyBypassFIFOScenario predicate, which remains UNSAT as expected)\n- Vacuity: None\n\n=== REPAIR INSTRUCTIONS ===\n- Identify and revert only the changes affecting role assignment and delegation clearance enforcement that led to the failure of assertRoleAssignmentClearance and assertDelegationClearance. Specifically:\n  - Move the clearance enforcement for role assignment (formerly a fact) back into the model as a fact, not just as an assertion:\n    ```\n    fact RoleAssignmentClearance {\n        all s: State, u: User, r: Role |\n            r in s.userRoles[u] => leqClearance[r.minClearance, u.clearance]\n    }\n    ```\n  - Similarly, restore the clearance check for delegations as a fact:\n    ```\n    fact DelegationClearance {\n        all d: Delegation | leqClearance[d.role.minClearance, d.to.clearance]\n    }\n    ```\n- Retain the Emergency mutex relaxation logic and all other Emergency module changes as-is.\n- After restoration, keep the corresponding assertions for negative/edge-case checking, but ensure the clearance constraints are enforced globally via facts.\n- Confirm that the EmergencyBypassFIFOScenario predicate remains unsatisfiable—do not attempt to fix this scenario until all regressions are resolved.\n\n=== ASSUMPTIONS REVIEW ===\nNone - assumptions appear sound\n\n=== REQUIREMENT UPDATES ===\nNone - requirements are clear\n\n=== UPDATED USER QUESTIONS ===\nNone\n\n=== Q&A STATUS UPDATE ===\nNone - no status changes\n\n=== HANDOFF TO RE ===\nPriority 1 (Critical blockers): \n- Revert only the changes that removed or relaxed clearance enforcement on role assignment and delegation (restore as facts).\n- Ensure assertion failures (assertRoleAssignmentClearance, assertDelegationClearance) are resolved and no new regressions are introduced.\n\nPriority 2 (Important improvements): \n- After regression is fixed, review EmergencyBypassFIFOScenario unsat status for possible future refinement.\n\nPriority 3 (Optional enhancements): \n- Consider additional negative/edge-case assertions for delegation and role assignment clearance in future iterations, once baseline behavior is stable.\n```",
