    "evaluator_feedback": "```\n=== NEXT ACTION DECISION ===\nDecision: refine/narrow fix\nRationale: The latest changes have not resolved the open issues: mutex role relaxation in Emergency mode is still too restrictive, and liveness for request processing is not enforced. Prior attempts have repeated similar strategies; alternative targeted corrections are now needed.\n\n=== VERIFICATION STATUS ===\n- Syntax: OK\n- Baseline: Satisfiable\n- Combined Model: Satisfiable\n- Assertions: Counterexamples (assertMutexAllowedDuringEmergency, assertAllRequestsEventuallyProcessed)\n- Instances: Meaningful for passing cases; failing assertions highlight missing/incorrect behaviors\n- Vacuity: None\n\n=== REPAIR INSTRUCTIONS ===\n1. DelegationMutex Fact (Emergency Mutex Relaxation):\n   - Refine the fact to explicitly permit a user to hold a mutex pair of roles in Emergency mode only if at least one role is held via delegation (direct assignment of both remains forbidden at all times).\n   - Update the DelegationMutex fact as follows:\n     ```\n     fact DelegationMutex {\n         // In all modes, direct assignment of mutex roles is forbidden\n         all s: State | all u: User | all r1, r2: Role |\n             r2 in r1.mutexWith => not (r1 in directRoles[s, u] and r2 in directRoles[s, u])\n         // In Normal mode, mutex roles forbidden (both direct and delegated)\n         all s: State | s.mode = Normal =>\n             all u: User | all r1, r2: Role |\n                 r2 in r1.mutexWith => not (r1 in s.userRoles[u] and r2 in s.userRoles[u])\n         // In Emergency mode, mutex roles allowed only if at least one held via delegation\n         all s: State | s.mode = Emergency =>\n             all u: User | all r1, r2: Role |\n                 r2 in r1.mutexWith =>\n                     not (r1 in s.userRoles[u] and r2 in s.userRoles[u])\n                     or (some d: Delegation | d.to = u and d in s.activeDelegations and (d.role = r1 or d.role = r2))\n     }\n     ```\n   - Rationale: This ensures that in Emergency, mutex roles can be held together only if delegation is involved, matching requirements.\n\n2. Liveness Constraint for Request Processing (All Requests Eventually Processed):\n   - Add a liveness fact to guarantee that every request is eventually processed in some Normal mode state.\n   - Example addition:\n     ```\n     fact AllRequestsEventuallyProcessed {\n         all r: Request | some s: State | s.mode = Normal and s.reqStatus[r] = Processed\n     }\n     ```\n   - Alternatively, if temporal patterns are needed, ensure that the system cannot reach a dead-end where requests remain perpetually pending.\n\n3. Regression Guard:\n   - Ensure that existing passing assertions (assertRoleAssignmentClearance, assertDelegationClearance, etc.) remain stable after implementing the above fixes.\n\n=== ASSUMPTIONS REVIEW ===\nNone - assumptions appear sound\n\n=== REQUIREMENT UPDATES ===\nNone - requirements are clear\n\n=== UPDATED USER QUESTIONS ===\nNone\n\n=== Q&A STATUS UPDATE ===\nNone - no status changes\n\n=== HANDOFF TO RE ===\nPriority 1 (Critical blockers): \n- Refine DelegationMutex fact to allow mutex pairs via delegation in Emergency, as per the requirements.\n- Add explicit liveness constraint ensuring all requests are eventually processed after Emergency ends.\n\nPriority 2 (Important improvements): \n- Confirm that regression does not occur on passing assertions.\n\nPriority 3 (Optional enhancements): \n- After fixes, consider adding negative/vacuity checks to confirm that mutex relaxation and liveness are not over-permissive.\n```",
