    "evaluator_feedback": "```\n=== NEXT ACTION DECISION ===\nDecision: refine/narrow fix\nRationale: User review adds important domain constraints—prohibiting self-delegation and self-approval, and clarifying direct role assignment behavior. Model constraints must be refined to enforce these requirements and address the mutex violation.\n\n=== VERIFICATION STATUS ===\n- Syntax: OK\n- Baseline: Satisfiable\n- Combined Model: Satisfiable\n- Assertions: Counterexamples (assertMutexAllowedDuringEmergency fails—mutex violation occurs in Normal mode)\n- Instances: Meaningful (counterexample is relevant and highlights the issue)\n- Vacuity: None\n\n=== CONVERGENCE_RECOMMENDATION ===\nStatus: FALSE\nReasoning: Model does not enforce all user-stated constraints (e.g., self-delegation/approval prohibition, mutex on direct assignment, clearance checks). Assertion failures and new user requirements necessitate further refinement.\n\n=== REPAIR INSTRUCTIONS ===\n- In fact DelegationMutex:\n  1. Forbid any user from holding two mutually exclusive roles through direct assignment in any mode:\n    ```\n    all s: State | all u: User | all r1, r2: Role |\n      r2 in r1.mutexWith =>\n        not (r1 in directRoles[s, u] and r2 in directRoles[s, u])\n    ```\n  2. In Normal mode, forbid any user from holding a pair of mutually exclusive roles (direct or via delegation):\n    ```\n    all s: State | s.mode = Normal =>\n      all u: User | all r1, r2: Role |\n        r2 in r1.mutexWith =>\n          not (r1 in s.userRoles[u] and r2 in s.userRoles[u])\n    ```\n  3. In Emergency mode, allow a user to hold a mutex pair only if at least one such role is held via delegation (but never via direct assignment of both):\n    ```\n    all s: State | s.mode = Emergency =>\n      all u: User | all r1, r2: Role |\n        r2 in r1.mutexWith =>\n          not (r1 in s.userRoles[u] and r2 in s.userRoles[u])\n          or (some d: Delegation | d.to = u and d in s.activeDelegations and (d.role = r1 or d.role = r2))\n    ```\n- Add fact to prohibit self-delegation:\n    ```\n    all d: Delegation | d.from != d.to\n    ```\n- Add fact to prohibit self-approval of requests:\n    ```\n    all r: Request | r.submitter != r.processor\n    ```\n- Add fact to enforce processor clearance is strictly greater than both request classification and submitter clearance:\n    ```\n    all r: Request | \n      r.processor.clearance > r.classification and\n      r.processor.clearance > r.submitter.clearance\n    ```\n- After all changes, rerun all assertions (especially mutex, delegation, and request-processing assertions) to confirm correctness.\n\n=== ASSUMPTIONS REVIEW ===\nNone - assumptions appear sound\n\n=== REQUIREMENT UPDATES ===\nNone - requirements are clear\n\n=== UPDATED USER QUESTIONS ===\nNone\n\n=== Q&A STATUS UPDATE ===\nNone - no status changes\n\n=== HANDOFF TO RE ===\nPriority 1 (Critical blockers):\n- Update DelegationMutex and request-processing logic as detailed above to enforce: no self-delegation, no self-approval, proper mutex enforcement (both modes), and clearance rules.\nPriority 2 (Important improvements):\n- Rerun all assertions, especially mutual exclusion, delegation, and request approval, to verify all user and security requirements are enforced.\nPriority 3 (Optional enhancements):\n- Add negative test cases to ensure no future regression on self-delegation, self-approval, and clearance ordering.\n```",
