    "evaluator_feedback": "```\n=== NEXT ACTION DECISION ===\nDecision: refine/narrow fix\nRationale: User review introduced new, high-priority requirements for request processing and clarified constraints for both Normal and Emergency modes, requiring substantial model updates. The model must be revised to address these process and role-handling behaviors.\n\n=== VERIFICATION STATUS ===\n- Syntax: OK\n- Baseline: Satisfiable\n- Combined Model: Satisfiable\n- Assertions: Counterexamples (assertMutexAllowedDuringEmergency fails; request processing, FIFO/priority, and admin credential assertions not yet modeled or covered)\n- Instances: Meaningful for prior scope, but missing new request-processing and credential update scenarios\n- Vacuity: None\n\n=== CONVERGENCE_RECOMMENDATION ===\nStatus: FALSE\nReasoning: The model does not cover key newly stated requirements (FIFO and processor recording in Normal, simultaneous processing of top-priority requests in Emergency, eventual processing, and no forced admin credential update in Normal). Assertions and scenarios for these are missing or failing, so further refinement is required.\n\n=== REPAIR INSTRUCTIONS ===\n- Update the model to explicitly represent requests, their classification (High/Medium/Low), and their processing state.\n- For Normal mode:\n  - Ensure that requests are processed strictly FIFO.\n  - Record which processor handles each request.\n  - Do not require the Admin to update credentials during Normal operation—remove or relax any such constraints.\n- For Emergency mode:\n  - Implement logic so that, in each Emergency transition, all pending requests of the highest classification are processed simultaneously.\n  - Ensure lower-classification requests are not processed until all higher ones are complete.\n  - Guarantee that all requests are eventually processed (liveness).\n- Add assertions to check that:\n  - FIFO is maintained in Normal mode.\n  - Processor recording is enforced per request.\n  - No unnecessary Admin credential update is required during Normal.\n  - In Emergency mode, all simultaneous processing rules and priorities are respected.\n- Re-verify the mutex role delegation logic in Emergency, ensuring the required scenario is enabled as previously described.\n- Review and, if needed, adjust the initial state and transitions to enable these behaviors without overconstraint.\n\n=== ASSUMPTIONS REVIEW ===\nNone - assumptions appear sound\n\n=== REQUIREMENT UPDATES ===\n- Clarify, document, and add formal statements for:\n  - FIFO processing and processor assignment in Normal mode.\n  - Emergency-mode group processing of top-priority requests and priority ordering.\n  - Eventual processing (liveness) for all requests.\n  - Explicitly state that Admin credential update is not required in Normal mode.\n\n=== UPDATED USER QUESTIONS ===\nNone\n\n=== Q&A STATUS UPDATE ===\nNone - no status changes\n\n=== HANDOFF TO RE ===\nPriority 1 (Critical blockers): \n- Model and assert FIFO processing with per-request processor recording in Normal mode.\n- Enforce Emergency-mode simultaneous processing of all highest-classification requests and proper priority ordering.\n- Ensure model does not require Admin credential update in Normal mode.\n- Enable and witness mutex role delegation scenario in Emergency as previously specified.\nPriority 2 (Important improvements):\n- Add liveness/property to ensure eventual processing of all requests.\n- Audit all transitions and constraints for overconstraint that blocks required processing or delegation scenarios.\nPriority 3 (Optional enhancements):\n- Add scenario-generation predicates for complex Emergency and Normal mode request-processing behaviors.\n```",
