    "evaluator_feedback": "```\n=== NEXT ACTION DECISION ===\nDecision: refine/narrow fix\nRationale: User has provided new requirements and clarifications that identify missing or incorrect constraints in the current model, requiring targeted refinement of facts and delegation logic.\n\n=== VERIFICATION STATUS ===\n- Syntax: OK\n- Baseline: Satisfiable\n- Combined Model: Satisfiable\n- Assertions: Counterexamples (assertMutexAllowedDuringEmergency fails; new constraints likely unverified)\n- Instances: Meaningful except for scenarios now revealed as underconstrained or incorrect\n- Vacuity: None\n\n=== CONVERGENCE_RECOMMENDATION ===\nStatus: FALSE\nReasoning: User-identified issues require additional model constraints and new scenario checks; hard metrics not satisfied due to counterexamples and incomplete coverage of newly clarified requirements.\n\n=== REPAIR INSTRUCTIONS ===\n- Update the Emergency session logic to enforce that only one session can have Emergency mode active at a time. \n    - Location: Fact or predicate governing Emergency state transitions.\n    - Example: Add a fact: `all s1, s2: Session | (s1 != s2 && s1.mode = Emergency && s2.mode = Emergency) => no` (or equivalent in Alloy).\n- Amend request submission constraint so that the submitter's clearance is at least as high as the request's classification (\"not less than\").\n    - Location: Fact related to request submission.\n    - Example: Replace `submitter.clearance > request.classification` with `submitter.clearance >= request.classification`.\n- Enforce that all processed requests must record a processor.\n    - Location: Fact or predicate on request processing.\n    - Example: Add `all r: Request | r.processed => some r.processor`.\n- Update delegation logic:\n    - Only allow delegation of roles (not arbitrary permissions or role extensions).\n    - Restrict delegation so that a user can only delegate a role if they themselves possess it, and only to users with lower or equal clearance.\n    - Example: Fact stating `all d: Delegation | d.delegator.clearance >= d.delegatee.clearance && d.role in d.delegator.roles`.\n- Refine DelegationMutex for Emergency mode per original instructions, but ensure changes do not violate above new constraints.\n    - Specifically, in Emergency, allow a user to hold both mutex roles if at least one is via delegation (and not both by direct assignment).\n\n=== ASSUMPTIONS REVIEW ===\n- Assumption: Only delegations can enable a user to hold both mutex roles in Emergency; direct assignment of both remains forbidden always.\n    - Category: keep\n    - Rationale: Matches requirements and user intent.\n\n- Assumption: Model's initial state or transitions allow necessary delegation scenarios.\n    - Category: confirm\n    - Rationale: Needs explicit validation after new constraints are added.\n\n- Assumption: Users can only delegate roles, not arbitrary extensions or permissions.\n    - Category: confirm\n    - Rationale: User clarified \"a user can only delegate a role EXTEND\" (interpret as roles only).\n\n- Assumption: Delegation permitted only to users with lower-or-same clearance.\n    - Category: confirm\n    - Rationale: Explicitly stated by user.\n\n=== REQUIREMENT UPDATES ===\n- Emergency mode must be unique per session: only one session in Emergency at a time.\n- Request submitter's clearance must be at least (not less than) request classification.\n- All processed requests must record a processor.\n- Delegation can only be for roles, and delegator must have equal or higher clearance than delegatee.\n\n=== UPDATED USER QUESTIONS ===\nNone\n\n=== Q&A STATUS UPDATE ===\nNone - no status changes\n\n=== HANDOFF TO RE ===\nPriority 1 (Critical blockers): \n- Add/adjust facts to ensure only one Emergency session at a time.\n- Correct submitter clearance check for request submission.\n- Require processor recording for all processed requests.\n- Restrict role delegation to only roles, only if delegator has role, and only to users of lower-or-equal clearance.\n- Refine DelegationMutex for Emergency as previously specified, ensuring constructive existential in Emergency state.\n\nPriority 2 (Important improvements): \n- Confirm that state initialization and transition logic admit required Emergency-mode delegation scenarios under new constraints.\n- Add/adjust test scenarios for each new or clarified requirement.\n\nPriority 3 (Optional enhancements): \n- Add constructive scenario predicate (e.g., MutexPossibleDuringEmergency) and validate it is not vacuously blocked under all constraints.\n```",
