    "evaluator_feedback": "```\n=== NEXT ACTION DECISION ===\nDecision: refine/narrow fix\nRationale: The current fixes introduced an unintended regression (assertDelegationClearance now fails) and the previous fix direction on DelegationMutex for Emergency is too broad or incomplete. Both counterexamples require targeted, narrowed corrections to their respective facts.\n\n=== VERIFICATION STATUS ===\n- Syntax: OK\n- Baseline: Satisfiable\n- Combined Model: Satisfiable\n- Assertions: Counterexamples (assertMutexAllowedDuringEmergency, assertDelegationClearance)\n- Instances: Meaningful (where found), but counterexamples indicate rule violation\n- Vacuity: None\n\n=== REPAIR INSTRUCTIONS ===\n1. DelegationMutex (Emergency Mode):\n   - Refine the Emergency mode branch to constructively allow a user to hold both mutex roles only if at least one is via delegation (never both direct), but ensure the logic does not inadvertently block the exact scenario the assertion requires. \n   - Explicitly check that at least one of the roles is held via a delegation present in s.activeDelegations (not just in userRoles).\n   - Example snippet for Emergency mode:\n     ```\n     all s: State | s.mode = Emergency =>\n       all u: User, r1, r2: Role | r2 in r1.mutexWith =>\n         not (r1 in directRoles[s, u] and r2 in directRoles[s, u]) and\n         (\n           (r1 in s.userRoles[u] and r2 in s.userRoles[u]) =>\n             (\n               (some d: Delegation | d.to = u and d.role in r1 + r2 and d in s.activeDelegations)\n             )\n         )\n     ```\n   - Remove any redundant or overlapping logic that could prevent the assertion's witness.\n\n2. DelegationConstraints:\n   - Strengthen the enforcement that a delegation can only be active in a state if the delegator holds the delegated role in that exact state, not just in some state.\n   - Replace:\n     ```\n     some s: State | d in s.activeDelegations => d.role in s.userRoles[d.from]\n     ```\n     with:\n     ```\n     all s: State | d in s.activeDelegations => d.role in s.userRoles[d.from]\n     ```\n   - This ensures that at any state where a delegation is active, the delegator holds the delegated role at that state.\n\n3. Regression Guard:\n   - After correcting the above, confirm that previously passing assertions (especially clearance, request lifecycle, and revocations) remain stable.\n\n=== ASSUMPTIONS REVIEW ===\nNone - assumptions appear sound\n\n=== REQUIREMENT UPDATES ===\nNone - no requirement updates justified\n\n=== UPDATED USER QUESTIONS ===\nNone\n\n=== Q&A STATUS UPDATE ===\nNone - no status changes\n\n=== HANDOFF TO RE ===\nPriority 1 (Critical blockers): \n- Refine DelegationMutex fact for Emergency mode as above to allow required mutex role combinations only via delegation.\n- Strengthen DelegationConstraints to require delegator holds the role in every state where the delegation is active.\nPriority 2 (Important improvements):\n- Regression guard: Ensure no unrelated behaviors or requirements are violated by the fix.\nPriority 3 (Optional enhancements):\n- None\n```",
