    "evaluator_feedback": "```\n=== NEXT ACTION DECISION ===\nDecision: refine/narrow fix\nRationale: User has clarified the intended behavior for Emergency-mode request processing, removing ambiguity in R3.2; the model and test scenario should now be updated to enforce strict concurrent processing of all higher-classification requests before any lower-classification requests.\n\n=== VERIFICATION STATUS ===\n- Syntax: OK\n- Baseline: Satisfiable\n- Combined Model: Satisfiable\n- Assertions: Pass\n- Instances: Meaningful (except EmergencyBypassFIFOScenario, which is unsat)\n- Vacuity: None\n\n=== CONVERGENCE_RECOMMENDATION ===\nStatus: FALSE\nReasoning: Model and scenario must be updated to reflect clarified requirement; current unsatisfiable scenario and requirement-model mismatch indicate further refinement is needed.\n\n=== REPAIR INSTRUCTIONS ===\nUpdate the Emergency-mode processing logic in the model (likely in the relevant predicate or function) to ensure that, during Emergency mode, all requests of the highest present classification are processed concurrently, and lower-classification requests are only processed after all higher-classification ones have been handled. Revise the EmergencyBypassFIFOScenario to expect and validate this strict classification-based processing order. Example: enforce that in any Emergency-mode step, requests with the highest classification are selected for processing, regardless of arrival order, and no lower-classification requests are processed until all higher ones are completed.\n\n=== ASSUMPTIONS REVIEW ===\n- Assumption: In Emergency mode, all pending requests with the highest classification are processed concurrently, and higher-classification requests always bypass (take precedence over) lower-classification requests, regardless of arrival order.\n- Category: confirm\n- Rationale: User has explicitly confirmed this assumption aligns with requirements; model should now accurately encode this logic.\n\n=== REQUIREMENT UPDATES ===\n- Affected Requirement/Assumption/Constraint: R3.2 (Emergency-mode request processing and FIFO bypass)\n- Issue Type: ambiguity (resolved)\n- Evidence: User clarification provided—higher-classification requests must always be processed before lower-classification requests in Emergency mode, without exception.\n- Recommended Update: Update R3.2 to explicitly state: \"During Emergency mode, all pending requests of the highest classification (High > Medium > Low) must be processed concurrently before any lower-classification requests, regardless of arrival order.\"\n- Implication: Model and scenarios must enforce this strict priority, eliminating ambiguity and aligning verification with the clarified requirement.\n\n=== UPDATED USER QUESTIONS ===\nNone\n\n=== Q&A STATUS UPDATE ===\nQ1: confirmed - User has clarified and confirmed Emergency-mode processing semantics; prior ambiguity is resolved.\n\n=== HANDOFF TO RE ===\nPriority 1 (Critical blockers): Update R3.2 to reflect clarified, strict classification-based Emergency-mode processing; revise model logic and test scenarios accordingly.\nPriority 2 (Important improvements): Ensure all relevant assumptions in the model documentation match updated requirement.\nPriority 3 (Optional enhancements): None\n```",
