 together and exclusively).\n- Category: confirm\n- Rationale: User has explicitly confirmed this behavior; assumption should now be enforced in the model.\n\n=== REQUIREMENT UPDATES ===\n- Affected Requirement/Assumption/Constraint: Emergency-mode request processing order (R3.2 and related operational description)\n- Issue Type: ambiguity (now resolved)\n- Evidence: User confirmation resolves prior ambiguity and aligns with group-processing semantics.\n- Recommended Update: Amend requirements documentation to state: \"During Emergency mode, all pending requests of the highest classification must be processed simultaneously and exclusively at each step until none remain; only then may lower-classification requests be processed simultaneously.\"\n- Implication: The model and all verification artifacts must enforce and test this group-processing rule, and any prior allowance for partial/individual processing must be removed.\n\n=== UPDATED USER QUESTIONS ===\nNone\n\n=== Q&A STATUS UPDATE ===\nQ1: confirmed - User has directly answered and resolved the Emergency-mode group processing semantics question.\n\n=== HANDOFF TO RE ===\nPriority 1 (Critical blockers): Update EmergencyBypassFIFOScenario predicate and EmergencyProcessingPriority fact to match confirmed group-processing requirement.\nPriority 2 (Important improvements): Add/adjust instance tests to verify group-processing transitions and ensure no partial/individual processing occurs in Emergency mode.\nPriority 3 (Optional enhancements): Review and extend Emergency-mode edge-case and liveness scenarios to ensure comprehensive verification under the clarified semantics.\n```",
