    "evaluator_feedback": "```\n=== NEXT ACTION DECISION ===\nDecision: escalate to requirement clarification\nRationale: Persistent unsatisfiability (UNSAT) of all positive scenario predicates—including the baseline—even after repeated model/scope relaxations and constraint adjustments, strongly indicates a requirement-level ambiguity, contradiction, or missing enabling assumption that must be clarified before further model repair is meaningful.\n\n=== VERIFICATION STATUS ===\n- Syntax: OK\n- Baseline: Unsatisfiable\n- Combined Model: Unsatisfiable\n- Assertions: Pass (no counterexamples)\n- Instances: N/A (no satisfying instances found)\n- Vacuity: None (predicates are UNSAT, not vacuously SAT)\n\n=== CONVERGENCE_RECOMMENDATION ===\nStatus: FALSE\nReasoning: Key predicates remain UNSAT, indicating unresolved requirement contradictions or ambiguities; no satisfying instances are found, and requirements cannot be considered verified.\n\n=== REPAIR INSTRUCTIONS ===\nNone – Model changes are not recommended until requirement-level ambiguities or contradictions are resolved. Further modeling work risks entrenching or masking the underlying requirements issue.\n\n=== ASSUMPTIONS REVIEW ===\n- Assumption: All combinations of user, role, and clearance assignments necessary for required scenarios are possible under current requirements and model scope.\n  - Category: confirm\n  - Rationale: Persistent UNSAT suggests that either the requirements or the model lack a necessary enabling assumption (e.g., about user clearance-role coverage, request submitter eligibility, or delegation preconditions) needed to realize even the baseline scenario.\n\n- Assumption: There are no implicit initial conditions, exceptions, or scenario-specific rules required to make the Emergency scenario (or baseline) possible.\n  - Category: confirm\n  - Rationale: The inability to realize any trace or scenario strongly suggests an unspoken but necessary initial condition or exception.\n\n=== REQUIREMENT UPDATES ===\n- Affected Requirement/Assumption/Constraint: Emergency mode scenario reachability and baseline system execution assumptions (see R3.2 and overall liveness/satisfiability).\n- Issue Type: ambiguity / missing requirement / logical gap\n- Evidence: All positive scenario predicates and baseline are UNSAT even after maximal model relaxation and scope adjustment, which cannot be explained by modeling error alone.\n- Recommended Update: Explicitly state any necessary enabling assumptions about initial user-role-clearance configuration, request submitter eligibility, object classification allocation, or any exceptions/initializations required to allow for the existence of a valid baseline execution and Emergency scenario (e.g., “For every classification, at least one user has sufficient clearance to submit a request, and at least one user is eligible to process every possible request under all required scenarios”).\n- Implication: Clarifying these requirements will prevent contradictory or incomplete system specifications, ensure model realizability, and allow Alloy verification to meaningfully cover required behaviors and scenarios. It may require relaxing or strengthening initial state or user/object assignment constraints, and will directly affect which behaviors are considered valid or required.\n\n=== UPDATED USER QUESTIONS ===\nAre there any implicit initial conditions, user-role-clearance combinations, or allowed exceptions that must be assumed (e.g., “there always exists a user with high clearance who is not the submitter of all required requests”) to make the baseline or Emergency scenarios possible? If so, please specify these explicitly, including any assumptions about the distribution of clearances, role assignments, or object classifications necessary for the system to realize its core scenarios.\n\n=== Q&A STATUS UPDATE ===\nNone - no status changes\n\n=== HANDOFF TO RE ===\nPriority 1 (Critical blockers): Requirement clarification—explicitly identify and specify any necessary enabling assumptions or missing constraints (initial user-role-clearance, request submitter/processor eligibility, object classification coverage) required for realizability of baseline and Emergency scenarios.\nPriority 2 (Important improvements): Review and update requirements to eliminate ambiguity or contradiction regarding system initialization, scenario reachability, and user/request/object coverage.\nPriority 3 (Optional enhancements): Once clarified, consider adding explicit requirement language or model comments to document these enabling assumptions for future verification and maintenance.\n```",
