ultiple requests in one step, and that the \"NoSelfApproval\" constraint only blocks self-approval, not all submitter/processor overlaps.\n\n=== POTENTIAL REQUIREMENT ISSUES ===\nNone – all previously identified ambiguities, gaps, and assumptions have been clarified by the user.\n\n=== ASSUMPTIONS REVIEW ===\nNone - assumptions appear sound\n\n=== REQUIREMENT UPDATES ===\nNone - no requirement updates justified\n\n=== UPDATED USER QUESTIONS ===\nNone\n\n=== Q&A STATUS UPDATE ===\n1: confirmed - User has explicitly confirmed all clarifications and provided direct answers.\n2: confirmed - User confirmed no implicit constraints on request distribution or timing.\n3: confirmed - User confirmed liveness and Emergency group-processing must always be realizable.\n4: confirmed - User confirmed no additional restrictions on user/role/clearance beyond stated requirements.\n\n=== HANDOFF TO RE ===\nPriority 1 (Critical blockers): \n- Review and repair the model encoding for Emergency group-processing and liveness in light of clarified requirements; resolve unsatisfiability in positive scenario predicates.\n- Ensure minimal scope is sufficient or explicitly add needed assumptions to guarantee realizability.\n\nPriority 2 (Important improvements): \n- Remove any unnecessary constraints in the model regarding request distribution, timing, and user/role/clearance combinations.\n\nPriority 3 (Optional enhancements): \n- Once model is SAT and all positive runs are satisfied, consider adding explicit negative/vacuity assertions to guard against future overconstraint and ensure meaningful coverage.\n```",
