    "evaluator_feedback": "```\n[DIAGNOSIS]:\nThe error \"The name 's' cannot be found\" at line 732, column 28, arises because in Alloy, multiple consecutive quantified expressions (e.g., 'some rH: Request | ... some rM: Request | ...') are interpreted as separate top-level formulas, not as sequential lines within a single block. Therefore, the scope of the variable 's' (defined as 'some s, s2: State | ...') does not extend to the subsequent 'some rM: Request | ...' and 'some rL: Request | ...' lines. Only the first line after the quantification sees 's'; the next lines are outside its scope, hence 's' is undefined there.\n\n[FIX INTENT]:\nCombine all enabling assumptions (for rH, rM, rL) within a single quantified block so that 's' and 's2' remain in scope for all sub-conditions.\n\n[REPAIR INSTRUCTIONS]:\n- Step 1: Replace the three separate quantifications for rH, rM, and rL (lines 731–733) with a single conjunction within the block of the 'some s, s2: State | ...' quantifier.\n- Step 2: Use 'and' to combine the existence of rH, rM, and rL (i.e., 'some rH: Request | ... and some rM: Request | ... and some rL: Request | ...') inside the same block.\n- Step 3: Ensure that all following lines (including the 'all r: Request | ...' constraint) remain within the scope of 's' and 's2' by enclosing the entire body in curly braces if not already.\n- Step 4: The corrected code should look like this:\n  ```\n  pred EmergencyBypassFIFOScenario {\n      some s, s2: State |\n          s.mode = Emergency and s2.mode = Emergency and Next[s, s2] and\n          some rH: Request | s.reqStatus[rH] = Pending and requestClassification[rH] = High and\n          some rM: Request | s.reqStatus[rM] = Pending and requestClassification[rM] = Medium and\n          some rL: Request | s.reqStatus[rL] = Pending and requestClassification[rL] = Low and\n          all r: Request |\n              ((s.reqStatus[r] = Pending and requestClassification[r] = High) => s2.reqStatus[r] = Processed and some s2.reqProcessor[r]) and\n              ((s.reqStatus[r] = Pending and requestClassification[r] != High) => s2.reqStatus[r] = Pending and s2.reqProcessor[r] = s.reqProcessor[r]) and\n              (s.reqStatus[r] = Processed => s2.reqStatus[r] = Processed and s2.reqProcessor[r] = s.reqProcessor[r])\n  }\n  ```\n  (Note that there are no line breaks or separate quantifiers for rM and rL; all are within the same conjunction.)\n\n[RATIONALE]:\nThis fix is Alloy 6 compliant because it ensures all relevant variables are within the scope of 's' and 's2', and it differs from prior failed attempts by unifying the enabling assumptions into a single block, rather than attempting to chain separate quantifiers.\n\n[LESSON]:\nWhen needing multiple existential conditions within the same scope in Alloy, combine them in a single quantified block with 'and', rather than writing separate quantifications on new lines, to preserve variable scope.\n```",
